status: closed
goal: Find optimal exit configuration specifically for s65 (funding carry) and its wrappers (s72) and combos (s58+s65, s58+s72). The universal trail(1.5) deployment massively improved all-time return (+532K%) but worsened max DD (-4.7%→-6.7%) and hurt 1-month returns (-21%). s65 previously had the widest trail (4.0 ATR) of any strategy — funding carry may need different exit treatment than momentum.
started: 2026-03-15
type: research+implementation
trigger: |
  Exit ablation deployed trail_mult=1.5 universally. For s65 specifically:
  - ALL TIME:  +532K% return improvement, but DD -4.7%→-6.7% (MIXED+)
  - 12 MONTHS: +2.3K% return, DD -3.3%→-1.8% (BETTER)
  - 3 MONTHS:  +101% return, DD -5.0%→-0.8% (BETTER)
  - 1 MONTH:   -21% return degradation (WORSE)
  s72 (s65+time_trail) shows same pattern: -22% at 1mo.
  s58+s65: -12% at 3mo, -22% at 1mo (the only WORSE portfolio at 3mo).
  s58+s72: -37% at 1mo, DD -1.6%→-5.3% (worst 1mo regression of any portfolio).

  s65 had trail_mult=4.0 (widest of any strategy). Funding carry generates
  steady income from funding payments — wider trails let carry accumulate.
  The 1.5 ATR trail may be cutting carry trades before they collect enough
  funding to justify the position.
baseline:
  s65_old_trail: 4.0 ATR (widest of any strategy)
  s65_new_trail: 1.5 ATR (universal default)
  s65_old_trail_schedule: [[0,3.0],[1,2.5],[2,2.0],[3,1.5]] (progressive)
  s65_new_trail_schedule: None
  s65_breakeven: 0.5 ATR (universal)
  s65_stop_mult: 4.5 (wider than momentum strategies)
  s65_no_stop_bars: 48 (wider protection — carry needs time)
  s65_min_hold: 24 (longer than momentum)
  s65_max_hold: 336 (14 days)
  affected_portfolios: [s65, s72, s58+s65, s58+s72]
progress: |
  PHASE 1 COMPLETE — trail_mult sweep (1.5, 2.0, 2.5, 3.0, 3.5, 4.0)
  Also tested 3 progressive schedules: 3.0→1.5, 4.0→2.0, 3.0→2.0
  Tested on: s65_solo, s72, s58+s65, s58+s72 × 4 periods (60/12/3/1 month)
  144 total simulation runs. Results in results/v4/s65_exit_sweep.json.

  FINDINGS:
  F1. trail(1.5) IS the best overall config (harmonic rank #1 for all 4 portfolios)
  F2. trail(4.0) [old] is consistently WORST at long periods — confirms exit ablation correct
  F3. The 1-month regression is ONLY in combo portfolios, not solo s65:
      - s65_solo 1mo: trail(1.5) = #2 Calmar (257.06) — FINE
      - s58+s65 1mo: trail(1.5) = #8 Calmar (5.88, DD -6.61%) — BAD
      - s58+s72 1mo: trail(1.5) = #7 Calmar (4.31, DD -7.14%) — BAD
  F4. Progressive schedule prog:3.0→1.5 beats current at ALL-TIME:
      - Solo Calmar: 144.63 vs 104.17 (+38%), DD: -2.77% vs -4.09% (better)
      - But 35% less return (1.55M% vs 2.07M%)
      - Consistently top-3 at all periods
  F5. s58+s72 has unique problem: trail(1.5) is #8 at 3mo (DD -4.05%)
      This is the only portfolio where trail(1.5) fails at 3-month horizon.
  F6. Wider trails help combos at 1-month by keeping s65 positions open longer,
      providing diversification when other strategy trades are also in drawdown.

  HYPOTHESIS VERDICT: PARTIALLY WRONG
  - Carry does NOT need wider trails for steady-state income accumulation
  - trail(1.5) wins at all horizons for solo s65
  - The 1-month combo regression is a portfolio-level interaction effect,
    not a carry-specific exit timing issue
  - The tight trail in combos causes correlated position exits → DD spike
